<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Building the Rashba Effect from the Atom</title>

<style>
* {
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

html, body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #111827;
}

body {
    overflow: hidden;
}

/* ---------- MAIN APP ---------- */

#app {
    width: 100vw;
    height: 100vh;
    background: white;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
}

/* ---------- TOP BAR ---------- */

.topbar {
    height: 72px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: 0 38px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    background: white;
}

.title {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111827;
}

.step-counter {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #6b7280;
}

/* ---------- CONTENT ---------- */

.content {
    flex: 1;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
}

.step {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    padding: 34px 65px 90px;
    display: none;
    overflow-y: auto;
}

.step.active {
    display: block;
}

.step-title {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 32px;
    margin: 5px 0 8px;
    color: #111827;
}

.step-subtitle {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 17px;
    color: #6b7280;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
}

.description {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 18px auto;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.55;
}

/* ---------- NAVIGATION ---------- */

.navigation {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 72px;
    background: white;
    border-top: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 16px;
}

button {
    font-family: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
}

.nav-btn {
    padding: 11px 23px;
    border-radius: 7px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    background: white;
    color: #111827;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 600;
}

.nav-btn:hover {
    background: #f3f4f6;
}

.nav-btn.primary {
    background: #111827;
    color: white;
    border-color: #111827;
}

.nav-btn.primary:hover {
    background: #374151;
}

/* ---------- VISUAL CONTAINERS ---------- */

.visual {
    max-width: 1000px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    min-height: 350px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

.panel {
    max-width: 950px;
    margin: 20px auto;
    padding: 20px 25px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #fafafa;
}

.highlight {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 20px auto;
    padding: 18px 25px;
    border-left: 4px solid #111827;
    background: #f9fafb;
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.5;
}

/* ---------- ATOM ---------- */

.atom {
    width: 310px;
    height: 310px;
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
}

.nucleus {
    width: 85px;
    height: 85px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #374151;
    color: white;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-weight: bold;
    z-index: 3;
}

.orbit {
    position: absolute;
    border: 1px dashed #9ca3af;
    border-radius: 50%;
}

.orbit.one {
    width: 180px;
    height: 180px;
}

.orbit.two {
    width: 275px;
    height: 275px;
}

.electron {
    position: absolute;
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    background: #2563eb;
    border-radius: 50%;
    z-index: 4;
}

.electron.e1 {
    top: 42px;
    left: 145px;
}

.electron.e2 {
    right: 15px;
    top: 145px;
}

.electron.e3 {
    bottom: 38px;
    left: 145px;
}

.spin-arrow {
    position: absolute;
    font-size: 34px;
    color: #2563eb;
    top: 6px;
    right: 90px;
}

/* ---------- SOC ---------- */

.flow {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 18px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.flow-box {
    min-width: 150px;
    padding: 20px 15px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    border-radius: 10px;
    text-align: center;
    background: white;
    font-weight: 600;
}

.arrow {
    font-size: 30px;
    color: #6b7280;
}

.equation {
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 29px;
    margin: 22px 0;
    font-family: Georgia, serif;
}

.big-equation {
    font-size: 40px;
}

/* ---------- SYMMETRY ---------- */

.symmetry-grid {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 70px;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.structure {
    width: 260px;
    height: 240px;
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: white;
}

.atom-center {
    position: absolute;
    width: 62px;
    height: 62px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #374151;
    color: white;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    left: 99px;
    top: 89px;
    z-index: 2;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.ligand {
    position: absolute;
    width: 34px;
    height: 34px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #9ca3af;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: bold;
}

.l1 { left: 113px; top: 25px; }
.l2 { left: 113px; bottom: 25px; }
.l3 { left: 25px; top: 103px; }
.l4 { right: 25px; top: 103px; }

.asym .l1 {
    background: #2563eb;
}

.asym .l4 {
    background: #111827;
}

/* ---------- BANDS ---------- */

.band-container {
    width: 750px;
    height: 350px;
    position: relative;
    border-left: 2px solid #374151;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #374151;
}

.axis-label {
    position: absolute;
    color: #374151;
    font-size: 14px;
}

.axis-energy {
    left: -48px;
    top: 5px;
    transform: rotate(-90deg);
}

.axis-k {
    bottom: -35px;
    right: 350px;
}

.band {
    position: absolute;
    width: 520px;
    height: 3px;
    background: #111827;
    transform-origin: left center;
}

.parabola {
    width: 500px;
    height: 230px;
    position: absolute;
    left: 125px;
    bottom: 0;
    border-top: 3px solid #111827;
    border-radius: 50% 50% 0 0;
    transform: scaleY(0.9);
}

/* Rashba SVG */

.band-svg {
    width: 760px;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: 360px;
}

svg text {
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- CONTROLS ---------- */

.controls {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin: 20px auto;
}

.control-btn {
    padding: 9px 17px;
    border-radius: 7px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    background: white;
    font-size: 14px;
}

.control-btn.active {
    background: #111827;
    color: white;
}

/* ---------- SPECTRUM ---------- */

.spectrum {
    width: 760px;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: 330px;
}

.bump {
    transition: all 0.5s ease;
}

/* ---------- FINAL MAP ---------- */

.chain {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 20px auto;
}

.chain-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 15px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
}

.chain-box {
    padding: 17px 20px;
    border: 1px solid #d1d5db;
    border-radius: 9px;
    background: white;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
}

.chain-arrow {
    font-size: 25px;
    color: #6b7280;
}

/* ---------- RESPONSIVE ---------- */

@media(max-width: 800px) {

    .step {
        padding: 25px 20px 85px;
    }

    .step-title {
        font-size: 25px;
    }

    .description {
        font-size: 16px;
    }

    .topbar {
        padding: 0 18px;
    }

    .title {
        font-size: 15px;
    }

    .symmetry-grid {
        gap: 20px;
    }

    .visual {
        min-height: 280px;
    }
}
</style>
</head>

<body>

<div id="app">

    <div class="topbar">
        <div class="title">Building the Rashba Effect</div>
        <div class="step-counter" id="counter">1 / 12</div>
    </div>

    <div class="content">

        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 1
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step active">

            <h1 class="step-title">Start with the Atom</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                Before understanding Rashba splitting, understand the electron.
            </div>

            <div class="visual">

                <div class="atom">

                    <div class="orbit one"></div>
                    <div class="orbit two"></div>

                    <div class="nucleus">
                        + nucleus
                    </div>

                    <div class="electron e1"></div>
                    <div class="electron e2"></div>
                    <div class="electron e3"></div>

                    <div class="spin-arrow">↻</div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="description">

                An electron has <b>electric charge</b> and an intrinsic
                angular momentum called <b>spin</b>.

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                <b>First idea:</b>
                The electron is not simply a tiny charged ball.
                It also possesses an intrinsic spin degree of freedom.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 2
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">The Electron Feels an Electric Field</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                The positively charged nucleus creates an electric field.
            </div>

            <div class="visual">

                <svg width="600" height="330" viewBox="0 0 600 330">

                    <circle cx="300" cy="165" r="55"
                            fill="#374151"/>

                    <text x="300" y="171"
                          text-anchor="middle"
                          fill="white"
                          font-size="18">
                        + nucleus
                    </text>

                    <g stroke="#9ca3af" stroke-width="2"
                       marker-end="url(#arrow)">

                        <line x1="300" y1="90"
                              x2="300" y2="35"/>

                        <line x1="300" y1="240"
                              x2="300" y2="295"/>

                        <line x1="225" y1="165"
                              x2="170" y2="165"/>

                        <line x1="375" y1="165"
                              x2="430" y2="165"/>

                    </g>

                    <defs>
                        <marker id="arrow"
                                markerWidth="8"
                                markerHeight="8"
                                refX="5"
                                refY="3"
                                orient="auto">
                            <polygon points="0 0, 6 3, 0 6"
                                     fill="#9ca3af"/>
                        </marker>
                    </defs>

                    <circle cx="430" cy="90"
                            r="11"
                            fill="#2563eb"/>

                    <text x="450" y="95"
                          font-size="16">
                        electron
                    </text>

                </svg>

            </div>

            <div class="description">

                The electron moves through the strong electric field
                produced by the nucleus.

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                The electric field becomes especially strong close to
                a <b>heavy nucleus</b>.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 3
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">Spin–Orbit Coupling</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                The electron's motion and spin interact.
            </div>

            <div class="flow">

                <div class="flow-box">
                    Electric field
                </div>

                <div class="arrow">→</div>

                <div class="flow-box">
                    Electron motion
                </div>

                <div class="arrow">→</div>

                <div class="flow-box">
                    Effective magnetic field
                </div>

                <div class="arrow">→</div>

                <div class="flow-box">
                    Spin interaction
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="equation">
                \(H_{\mathrm{SOC}}\propto\mathbf{L}\cdot\mathbf{S}\)
            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                <b>Spin–orbit coupling (SOC)</b> is the interaction between
                the electron's spin and its orbital motion in the electric
                field of the nucleus.

            </div>

            <div class="description">

                Heavy elements such as <b>Pb</b> have strong SOC because
                the electric field near their nuclei is very strong.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 4
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">SOC Alone Is Not Enough</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                We now introduce the second ingredient: inversion symmetry.
            </div>

            <div class="symmetry-grid">

                <div>

                    <div class="structure">

                        <div class="atom-center">Pb</div>

                        <div class="ligand l1">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l2">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l3">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l4">X</div>

                    </div>

                    <p style="text-align:center;">
                        Symmetric environment
                    </p>

                </div>

                <div style="font-size:40px;">
                    ⇄
                </div>

                <div>

                    <div class="structure">

                        <div class="atom-center">Pb</div>

                        <div class="ligand l1">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l2">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l3">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l4">X</div>

                    </div>

                    <p style="text-align:center;">
                        Inverted environment
                    </p>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="equation">

                \(V(\mathbf r)=V(-\mathbf r)\)

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                If the structure looks equivalent after inversion,
                <b>inversion symmetry is preserved</b>.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 5
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">Break Inversion Symmetry</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                Now make the environment different in opposite directions.
            </div>

            <div class="symmetry-grid">

                <div>

                    <div class="structure asym">

                        <div class="atom-center">Pb</div>

                        <div class="ligand l1">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l2">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l3">X</div>
                        <div class="ligand l4">I</div>

                    </div>

                    <p style="text-align:center;">
                        Inversion symmetry broken
                    </p>

                </div>

                <div style="font-size:40px;">
                    →
                </div>

                <div style="max-width:360px;">

                    <div class="panel">

                        <b>Asymmetric environment</b>

                        <p>
                            The potential is no longer the same in opposite
                            directions.
                        </p>

                        <div class="equation">
                            \[
                            V(\mathbf r)\neq V(-\mathbf r)
                            \]
                        </div>

                        <div class="equation">
                            \[
                            \nabla V\neq0
                            \]
                        </div>

                    </div>

                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                The crystal now provides an internal
                <b>potential gradient</b>.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 6
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">The Two Ingredients Meet</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                Rashba physics emerges from their combination.
            </div>

            <div class="flow">

                <div class="flow-box">
                    <b>Strong SOC</b>
                    <br><br>
                    Spin interacts with orbital motion.
                </div>

                <div class="arrow">+</div>

                <div class="flow-box">
                    <b>Inversion asymmetry</b>
                    <br><br>
                    The potential has a preferred direction.
                </div>

            </div>

            <div style="text-align:center;font-size:45px;margin:25px;">
                ↓
            </div>

            <div class="flow">

                <div class="flow-box">
                    Momentum
                </div>

                <div class="arrow">↔</div>

                <div class="flow-box">
                    Spin
                </div>

                <div class="arrow">→</div>

                <div class="flow-box">
                    <b>Spin–momentum coupling</b>
                </div>

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                <b>This is the central idea:</b>

                Strong SOC acting in a structure without inversion symmetry
                produces a momentum-dependent spin interaction.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 7
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">The Rashba Hamiltonian</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                The physics can now be written mathematically.
            </div>

            <div class="equation big-equation">

                \(H_R =
                \alpha_R
                (\mathbf{k}\times\hat{\mathbf z})
                \cdot\boldsymbol{\sigma}\)

            </div>

            <div class="panel">

                <p><b>\(\alpha_R\)</b> — Rashba coupling strength</p>

                <p><b>\(\mathbf{k}\)</b> — electron crystal momentum</p>

                <p><b>\(\hat{\mathbf z}\)</b> — direction associated with
                the structural asymmetry</p>

                <p><b>\(\boldsymbol{\sigma}\)</b> — spin operators</p>

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                The crucial feature is that the spin interaction depends
                on <b>momentum \(k\)</b>.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 8
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">From One Band to Rashba-Split Bands</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                Turn the Rashba interaction on and watch what happens.
            </div>

            <div class="controls">

                <button class="control-btn active"
                        id="socOff"
                        onclick="setBandMode('off')">
                    SOC OFF
                </button>

                <button class="control-btn"
                        id="socOn"
                        onclick="setBandMode('on')">
                    SOC + Asymmetry ON
                </button>

            </div>

            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;">

                <svg class="band-svg"
                     viewBox="0 0 760 360">

                    <line x1="80" y1="300"
                          x2="720" y2="300"
                          stroke="#374151"
                          stroke-width="2"/>

                    <line x1="80" y1="300"
                          x2="80" y2="35"
                          stroke="#374151"
                          stroke-width="2"/>

                    <text x="25" y="50"
                          font-size="15">
                        Energy
                    </text>

                    <text x="700" y="330"
                          font-size="15">
                        k
                    </text>

                    <!-- unsplit -->
                    <path id="singleBand"
                          d="M 160 265
                             Q 380 65 600 265"
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="#111827"
                          stroke-width="4"/>

                    <!-- split bands -->

                    <path id="upperBand"
                          d="M 160 250
                             Q 380 35 600 250"
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="#2563eb"
                          stroke-width="4"
                          opacity="0"/>

                    <path id="lowerBand"
                          d="M 160 280
                             Q 380 95 600 280"
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="#6b7280"
                          stroke-width="4"
                          opacity="0"/>

                    <circle cx="380"
                            cy="150"
                            r="6"
                            fill="#111827"/>

                </svg>

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                With the Rashba interaction, the original electronic
                states separate into two momentum-dependent branches:

                <div class="equation">
                    \(E_\pm(k)=E_0(k)\pm\alpha_R k\)
                </div>

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 9
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">The Splitting Is Spin-Dependent</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                The two branches carry different spin orientations.
            </div>

            <div style="display:flex;justify-content:center;">

                <svg class="band-svg"
                     viewBox="0 0 760 380">

                    <line x1="80" y1="320"
                          x2="720" y2="320"
                          stroke="#374151"
                          stroke-width="2"/>

                    <line x1="80" y1="320"
                          x2="80" y2="30"
                          stroke="#374151"
                          stroke-width="2"/>

                    <path d="M 150 275
                             Q 370 40 620 250"
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="#2563eb"
                          stroke-width="4"/>

                    <path d="M 150 295
                             Q 370 105 620 275"
                          fill="none"
                          stroke="#6b7280"
                          stroke-width="4"/>

                    <!-- spin arrows -->

                    <text x="230" y="160"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#2563eb">
                        ↑
                    </text>

                    <text x="300" y="100"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#2563eb">
                        ↗
                    </text>

                    <text x="430" y="110"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#2563eb">
                        →
                    </text>

                    <text x="520" y="160"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#2563eb">
                        ↘
                    </text>

                    <text x="230" y="300"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#6b7280">
                        ↓
                    </text>

                    <text x="320" y="285"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#6b7280">
                        ↙
                    </text>

                    <text x="430" y="285"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#6b7280">
                        ←
                    </text>

                    <text x="520" y="300"
                          font-size="28"
                          fill="#6b7280">
                        ↖
                    </text>

                    <text x="100" y="50"
                          font-size="15">
                        Energy
                    </text>

                    <text x="700" y="345"
                          font-size="15">
                        k
                    </text>

                </svg>

            </div>

            <div class="highlight">

                Changing momentum changes the preferred spin orientation.
                This produces a characteristic <b>spin texture</b>
                around the Rashba-split bands.

            </div>

        </section>


        <!-- =====================================================
             STEP 10
        ====================================================== -->

        <section class="step">

            <h1 class="step-title">A Real Perovskite Is More Complicated</h1>

            <div class="step-subtitle">
                The simple Rashba model is only the beginning.
            </div>

            <div class="visual">

                <svg width="760"
                     height="330"
                     viewBox="0 0 760 330">

                    <!-- Pb atoms -->

                    <g fill="#374151">

                        <circle cx="180" cy="100" r="32"/>
                        <circle cx="380" cy="100" r="32"/>
                        <circle cx="580" cy="100" r="32"/>

                        <circle cx="180" cy="240" r="32"/>
                        <circle cx="380" cy="240" r="32"/>
                        <circle cx="580" cy="240" r="32"/>

                    </g>

                    <!-- I atoms -->

                    <g fill="#9ca3af">

                        <circle cx="280" cy="100" r="20"/>
                        <circle cx="480" cy="100" r="20"/>

                        <circle cx="280" cy="240" r="20"/>
                        <circle cx="480" cy="240" r="20"/>

                        <circle cx="180" cy="170" r="20"/>
                        <circle cx="380" cy="170" r="20"/>
